          syntax: `try:\n    result = risky_operation()\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f"Bad value: {e}")\nexcept FileNotFoundError as e:\n    print(f"File missing: {e}")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f"Unexpected: {e}")`,
          example: `def parse_row(row):\n    try:\n        return {\n            "id":     int(row["id"]),\n            "amount": float(row["amount"]),\n        }\n    except (ValueError, KeyError) as e:\n        return None\n\nrows = [\n    {"id": "1",   "amount": "150.0"},\n    {"id": "bad", "amount": "200.0"},\n    {"id": "3",   "amount": "abc"},\n]\n\ngood, bad = 0, 0\nfor r in rows:\n    if parse_row(r):\n        good += 1\n    else:\n        bad += 1\n\nprint(f"Parsed: {good}, Failed: {bad}")`,
