            question: 'What does extrasaction="ignore" do in csv.DictWriter?',
            answer: 'By default DictWriter raises ValueError if a row dict has keys not in fieldnames. extrasaction="ignore" silently drops extra keys. Useful when your transform rows have extra debugging fields you do not want in the output.',
