          practice: 'Write a run(config) function that takes a dict with keys "date", "env", and "batch_size". It should simulate extracting batch_size rows, log the count, and return {"status":"ok","rows":N}. Wrap it in try/except returning {"status":"error","error":str(e)} on failure.',
          hint: 'Use config.get("batch_size", 1000) with a default. Return a dict either way. Use logging.getLogger() for structured output.',
          solution: `import logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format="%(levelname)s: %(message)s")\nlog = logging.getLogger("pipeline")\n\ndef run(config):\n    date       = config.get("date", "unknown")\n    env        = config.get("env", "dev")\n    batch_size = config.get("batch_size", 1000)\n    try:\n        log.info(f"Starting — date={date}, env={env}, batch={batch_size}")\n        rows = list(range(batch_size))  # simulate extract\n        log.info(f"Processed {len(rows):,} rows")\n        return {"status": "ok", "rows": len(rows)}\n    except Exception as e:\n        log.error(str(e))\n        return {"status": "error", "error": str(e)}\n\nprint(run({"date": "2024-01-15", "env": "prod", "batch_size": 500}))`,
